index 000000000..ae409c30a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/platform/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Platform release boundary
+
+The `bc-platform` release line covers shared BigCherry capabilities:
+build and patch orchestration, engine-independent configuration, release
+tooling, hardware discovery, and common benchmark and validation interfaces.
+It does not represent a newly qualified Radiance or llama.cpp engine build.
+
+A meaningful change to the shared platform is deliberately included in this
+release line by adding a short file under `platform/changes/` in the **same
+commit** as the change. Use a `feat(platform):`, `fix(platform):` or
+`perf(platform):` commit subject. See the
+[change-entry instructions](ENTRY_GUIDE.md). A single mixed commit may
+describe both engine and shared-platform changes, but engine-specific work alone must not
+create a platform marker.
+
+Release-please watches only `platform/changes/` and excludes
+`platform/changes/release-state/`. Only a change-entry file triggers a new
+platform release. This
+explicit boundary is necessary: its `exclude-paths` option cannot ignore
+an engine commit that also edits files outside the engine directory.
+
+Once a platform change is merged into `main`, release-please proposes a
+`bc-platform` release PR, collecting platform changes since the previous
+release. The version and GitHub release are published only when that PR is
+merged. Updating the engine pins, adding model evidence, or merging an
+engine-specific PR does not by itself publish a platform release.
+
+[The release process](../docs/reference/build/RELEASES.md) describes the
+tags and changelog. The old root-scoped platform release history is retained
+under [the archived changelog](../docs/releases/PLATFORM_CHANGELOG.md);
+historical entries may contain engine-specific changes.
